performance compared to unimodal data. In addition, the FKG-MM framework is based on the fuzzy knowledge graph model, one of the models that represent and compute effectively with medical data in tabular form. Through some experiment scenarios utilizing the well-known BRSET dataset on multi-modal diabetic retinopathy, it has been experimentally validated that the feature selection method, when combining image features with tabular medical data features, gives the highest reliability results among 5 methods including Feature Selection Method, Tensor Product, Hadamard Product, Filter Selection, and Wrapper Selection. In addition, the experiment also confirms that the accuracy of FKG-MM increases by 12–14% when combining image data with tabular medical data than the related methods diagnosing only on tabular data.",exclude_uncertain_unstable,EXCLUDE,EC2_no_text_component,,primary_model_paper,no,no,no,no,,,,,"The abstract describes a new multi-modal fuzzy knowledge graph framework integrating clinical records, X‑Ray images, and tabular medical data, indicating a biological modality, but it does not mention any natural‑language text, prompts, or text‑bio mapping. | The abstract proposes a fuzzy knowledge graph for multimodal data integration but mentions no decoder, autoregressive, or other generative mechanism, and provides no evidence of broad pretraining or transferable representations.","The abstract describes a new multi-modal fuzzy knowledge graph framework integrating clinical records, X‑Ray images, and tabular medical data, indicating a biological modality, but it does not mention any natural‑language text, prompts, or text‑bio mapping.","The abstract proposes a fuzzy knowledge graph for multimodal data integration but mentions no decoder, autoregressive, or other generative mechanism, and provides no evidence of broad pretraining or transferable representations.",
./analysis/cross_agent_screening_agreement_current_3ds_2gpt/cross_model_decisions.csv:121: This study demonstrates that multi-modal MRIs can successfully identify glioblastoma subtypes characterized by deep learning derived radiomic features. Future work will focus on validation with comprehensive molecular and tissue-based profiles, survival outcomes, and treatment responses to support personalized medicine.",exclude_uncertain_unstable,EXCLUDE,application_wrapper,,application_wrapper,no,no,no,yes,none,none,"Masked Auto-Encoder (MAE), a deep learning architecture trained through self-supervised learning",clear_exclude,"The abstract describes a deep learning-based radiomic subtyping study using MAE for feature extraction and clustering, with no natural-language text component, no text-bio bridge, and no generative mechanism; it is an application wrapper and not eligible.",This paper uses a Masked Auto-Encoder on MRI data for subtyping glioblastoma; no natural-language text component or text-bio bridge is described.,"The paper uses a Masked Auto-Encoder for MRI feature extraction and clustering to identify glioblastoma subtypes, with no mention of generative text or biological sequence outputs. It does not describe a generative text-bio foundational model.","The abstract describes a deep learning-based radiomic subtyping study using MAE for feature extraction and clustering, with no natural-language text component, no text-bio bridge, and no generative mechanism; it is an application wrapper and not eligible.",IMG-33. Unveiling glioblastoma heterogeneity with deep learning derived MRI subtyping: insights from the global ReSPOND consortium,"This study aims to identify distinct imaging subtypes of glioblastoma using multi-modal MRIs from the ReSPOND consortium, providing insights into tumor heterogeneity to inform personalized treatment approaches.
