l for single-cell\""},{"record_id":"rec_000292","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a downstream self-training framework for cell-type annotation using outputs from a single-cell foundation model. The abstract does not describe a new generative model.","evidence_snippet":"\"self-training framework for cell type annotation\"; \"obtained from the single-cell foundation model\""},{"record_id":"rec_000293","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"TSProm adapts DNABERT2 to decode promoter regulatory logic and adds interpretability modules. That is a wrapper/adaptation around an existing foundation model, not a new generative foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"adapts a DNA foundation model (DNABERT2) to decode\"; \"explainable AI module\""},{"record_id":"rec_000294","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract centers on conditional optimal transport for response prediction and says it exploits the ESM protein language model. That is a predictive wrapper, not a generative model.","evidence_snippet":"\"Modeling ... response\"; \"exploited the ESM protein language model\""},{"record_id":"rec_000295","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"GC-MoE is a genomics-guided mixture-of-experts framework for histology-based spatial transcriptomics. The abstract only references a pretrained foundation model as supporting context, not as the candida