 discovery”"},{"record_id":"rec_000036","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract says this is a systematic review of AMR modeling across published studies. It synthesizes transformer-based and applied large language model systems rather than presenting one new model.","evidence_snippet":"“Following PRISMA 2020 guidelines, we systematically reviewed 156 records” and “we organize AMR modeling”"},{"record_id":"rec_000037","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes a platform that combines existing computational pipelines with LLMs to contextualize outputs and generate hypotheses. That is a wrapper/workflow around an LLM, not a standalone foundational model paper.","evidence_snippet":"“we introduce ... a novel cointelligent platform” and “LLMs ... contextualize algorithmic outputs or predictions”"},{"record_id":"rec_000038","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a new hybrid CNN-Transformer model for predicting TAD boundaries from DNA and epigenomic signals. The abstract does not describe a substantive text or language component.","evidence_snippet":"“we present CT-TADB, a hybrid CNN-Transformer framework that integrates DNA sequence with histone modification and CTCF binding signals”"},{"record_id":"rec_000039","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a bibliometric and visual analysis of AI in chronic kidney disease, based on published literature rather than a primary model. It summarizes trends and topics instead of proposing a new model.","evidence_snippet":"“Bibliometric and visual analysis of trends and future directions” and “888 relevant publications were analyzed”"},{"record_id":"rec_000040","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract reports workshop outcomes, community needs, and a portal resource, so it is a community/resource paper rather than a model paper. It does not describe a substantive text-bio model.","evidence_snippet":"“we report outcomes from the 2025 Summer Workshop” and “we established PlantSCHub, a community-curated web portal”"}]}
