tial transcriptomics, but the abstract centers on morphology and genomic knowledge, not a text/language component. No substantive text-bio bridge is described.","evidence_snippet":"“Histology-Based Single-Cell Spatial Transcriptomics” and “Genomic knowledge”"},{"record_id":"rec_000296","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"unclear","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The title and abstract read as a broad review of cardiac aging with multi-omics and computational approaches, not a new candidate model. Language-model-assisted methods are mentioned only as emerging approaches.","evidence_snippet":"“Decoding cardiac aging with multi-omics and computational approaches” and “emerging language-model–assisted approaches”"}]}
