_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This paper introduces a metric and benchmarking suite for biological foundation models, not a candidate model. It is therefore a benchmark/resource paper.","evidence_snippet":"\"introduce counterfactual consistency as a novel, model-agnostic metric\" and \"release an open-source benchmarking suite\""},{"record_id":"rec_000285","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"scAgent is framed as an agentic annotation framework based on LLMs for single-cell RNA-seq cell typing. The core use is applying an LLM-based wrapper to a downstream bio task.","evidence_snippet":"\"framework based on Large Language Models (LLMs)\" for \"single-cell RNA-seq\" cell type annotation"},{"record_id":"rec_000286","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The title presents a retrieval-augmented generation approach for spot-level niche typing using SpotTypeLLM. This is an applied LLM wrapper for spatial multi-omics annotation rather than a primary text-bio foundation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"Bi-View Retrieval-Augmented Generation With SpotTypeLLM\" for \"Spatial Multi-Omics\" annotation"},{"record_id":"rec_000287","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The model is a multi-modal diffusion system for multi-omics generation and translation. The abstract describes biological modalities only, with no text or language component.","evidence_snippet":"\"multi-omics data generation and translation\" and \"Dual-Cross-Attention\" between molecular modalities"},{"record_id":"rec_000288","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"RNABag is a transcriptome foundation model for precision oncology across biopsy modalities. The abstract is about transcriptomic representation learning and clinical prediction, not text-language modeling.","evidence_snippet":"\"Transcriptomic data\" and \"foundation model\" for \"precision oncology across biopsy modalities\""}]}
