onale":"This is a primary multimodal deep learning framework, but the modalities are biological features, transcriptomic states, and drug/cell contexts. The abstract does not describe any text-language component.","evidence_snippet":"“integrates … differential gene expression and kinase inhibition profiles” and “pathway-informed graph neural networks”"},{"record_id":"rec_000032","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract explicitly frames the paper as a state-of-the-art review of AI for cancer target discovery and drug development. It is survey-style rather than a primary text-bio model paper.","evidence_snippet":"“This review specifically examines how AI advances mechanistic cancer target discovery and translational drug development”"}]}
