ation model.","evidence_snippet":"\"these systems depend on the LLM for path traversal\" and \"the transcriptomic branch\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000412","paper_type":"benchmark_resource","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"benchmark_resource","uncertainty_reason":"text_bio_bridge_unclear","decision_rationale":"The title says this is an open-source toolkit for building and evaluating biomedical deep research agents, so it is a resource rather than a candidate model paper. It covers biomedical domains such as genomics, transcriptomics, and proteins, but the bridge to a specific text-bio model is not established.","evidence_snippet":"\"Open-source Toolkit for Building and Evaluating Biomedical Deep Research Agents\"; \"genomics and transcriptomics, proteins\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000413","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a primary generative diffusion-model paper for histopathological image translation with genomics/transcriptomics guidance. The abstract does not describe a substantive text/language component in the model itself.","evidence_snippet":"\"diffusion model-based framework\" and \"genomics-and/or transcriptomics-guided editing of histopathological images\"."},{"record_id":"rec_000414","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"mixed_signals","decision_rationale":"The title indicates a multimodal deep learning model for breast cancer risk evaluation using radiology and genomics. The abstract fragment mentions LLM only obliquely, but not as a substantive part of the candidate model.","evidence_snippet":"\"multimodal approaches—integrating different types of data, such as radiology and genomics\" and a stray \"LLM\" mention."},{"record_id":"rec_000415","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"unclear","text_bio_bridge_present":"unclear","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"mixed_signals","decision_rationale":"The title says this is a safety-centric perspective on AI in genomics, which points to commentary rather than a primary model paper. The abstract references generative genomic models, but not a specific text-bio model or bridge.","evidence_snippet":"\"A safety-centric perspective\" and \"generative genomic models\" in genomics."},{"record_id":"rec_000416","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"unclear","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"mixed_signals","decision_rationale":"The abstract describes an autonomous curation workflow for spatial omics archives, centered on evidence evaluation and standardization rather than a new text-bio foundation model. The agentic setup is a wrapper/workflow around curation tasks.","evidence_snippet":"\"Autonomous Spatial Omics Data Curation\" with \"schema-constrained evidence evaluation\" and a \"self-refining standardization agent\"."}]}
